The eternal fires, thought I to myself, and then inquired casuallywhat they=
 were. A moment before I had been filled withenthusiasm over this ruined ci=
ty and its fossilized remains.
A whilelater we turned round and looked at the lake.
Did not Issicore makea great journey to find you? If his wisdom bidshim vis=
it the Holy Isle, let him do so, my father. Had you aught to do with her de=
ath, Lord?
His coarse but handsome face grew cunning, and he smacked his lips.
I cut off thefinger of another who wished to shake hands with me when I had=
 toldhim to go away.
Also, as I have said, quite suddenly he had changed insome subtle fashion. =
Itwould be dangerous, no doubt, but at the least it would also beexciting. =
Hans, I said, keep your rifle ready, but dont shoot unless you areobliged. =
Did not Issicore makea great journey to find you?
Yes, Lord, when I was quite young before he became a priest. I understand, =
the priest replied, highly gratified, as his faceshewed.
Behold, he has sent you and now I implore youto save my daughter from the f=
ate that awaits her.
I understand thatyou will require payment in white and red stones, also in =
gold andivory. Is this thetime and place to chatter of pretty women? Lord, =
I answered that I would rather go to Heu-Heu. Now if some pretty lady were =
to come and tellthe Baas that he was oh! So now I think I will go to sleep,=
 and to-morrow or thenext day the Baas can save her.=20
